{
  "id": "2026-10-06-invisible-cochlear-implant",
  "title": "The first hearing implant you can't see at all is now reaching patients",
  "topic": "일상",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Today's story is about a hearing device that disappears completely under the skin.",
    "Cochlear implants have helped people with severe hearing loss for about fifty years.",
    "But until now, every user had to wear a piece of hardware behind the ear.",
    "That part holds the microphone and the battery, and you have to take it off to sleep or swim.",
    "An Austrian company called Med-El has now put the whole system inside the head.",
    "The new device weighs just twenty grams and sits right under the scalp.",
    "The hardest part was the microphone, because it has to pick up sound through skin and tissue.",
    "Engineers had been trying to crack that problem for decades.",
    "To charge it, users hold a small pod against their head for about an hour.",
    "One charge lasts up to forty hours.",
    "In a trial with thirty patients, people heard about as well as with a regular implant.",
    "What they loved most was being able to hear while sleeping, swimming, or playing sports.",
    "The first four patients have now received it in Europe, but it isn't approved in the U.S. yet.",
    "Next time you see someone with an earpiece, think about how much smaller this tech keeps getting. Have a great day!"
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "오스트리아 메드엘이 귀 뒤 외부 장치 없이 두피 아래에 전부 들어가는 인공와우를 처음 상용 이식했다.",
    "가장 어려운 건 피부 밑에서 소리를 받는 마이크였다. 20그램, 한 시간 충전으로 최대 40시간 쓴다.",
    "30명 임상에서 기존 제품만큼 들렸고, 자거나 수영할 때도 들린다는 점이 가장 호평받았다. 유럽에서만 승인됐다."
  ],
